17:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Standard Precautions treat blood, all body fluids except sweat, non-intact skin, and mucous membranes as potentially infectious — for every patient, in every encounter. The principle replaced an older approach that applied extra precautions only to patients known to be infectious, which failed for the obvious reason that most infectious patients are not known to be."}]
