19:["$","p","3",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Hand hygiene is the single most effective measure, and the one most often skipped under time pressure. The CDC identifies the moments that matter: before touching a patient, before a clean or aseptic procedure, after body fluid exposure risk, after touching a patient, and after touching the patient's surroundings."}]
